  "description": "YODYUP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C99 H82 Fe9 O19 Tb3 1-,2(C16 H36 N1 1+),Cl1 1-,C4 H10 O1,C4 H8 O1. From the CIF bond table, Fe1 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe8 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe9 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Fe12 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe10 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe11 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe13 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe14 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe15 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe16 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe17 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe18 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Tb11 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb12 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb13 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2' (Fe) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 21 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.804-3.877 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.67-109.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C131H154ClFe9N2O19Tb3. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
